 rate would be far lower than what's observed. Studies tracking bat hunting behavior show high capture rates (sometimes catching an insect every few seconds during peak feeding), which lines up with precise targeting, not random collision. So the visual impression of "erratic = blind" makes intuitive sense from a human perspective, but for bats, that erratic flight is actually a sign of highly tuned, active sensory tracking, not the absence of it.
